From 135da2b1be24758db45c1c84e2ee49f3f28893f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Warren Deng <warrdeng@meta.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 21:20:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] [Inductor] Preserve Triton cache-group formats during
 runtime transport

Triton #12001 replaced absolute child-path mappings with filename lists.
Runtime cache export rejected the new format, and recreating a mapping on
import changes the manifest bytes checked by strict Inductor reload.
Normalize both formats for validation and retain the producer representation
when hydrating cache groups. Legacy bundles default to path mappings.
Add direct roundtrip coverage for filename bytes and member order.

Authored with AI assistance (Codex) at Warren's request.

Test Plan:
```bash
podman exec triton-pin-202417 bash -c 'source /data/users/warrdeng/triton-pin/ci-202417/container_env.sh
python /data/users/warrdeng/triton-pin/pytorch-cache-transport/agent_space/verify_cache_transport.py'
spin quicklint
lintrunner -a
```
63 cases pass with each full native old/candidate Triton pin on H100 CUDA13.2,
using the changed transport source on the existing e6fb976 PyTorch wheel.
Full spin lint also attempted; the executorch C++ compatibility linter requires
a build directory absent from this Python-only worktree.
