From e5f825e00df233d8a90c1a27e695f855b1c5bfb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Warren Deng <warrdeng@meta.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:12:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Validate Triton runtime-cache member lists before
 hydration

A malformed kernel record could provide a dictionary for members. Header
validation checked its keys, but filename-format serialization wrote its
unchecked values. Import promoted that invalid group before rejecting it,
leaving an entry that blocked a corrected retry.

Reject non-list members during decoding, before cache directories are
created or populated. Existing member validation still checks every filename.
Add the mapping-members case to the damaged-bundle/no-write regression.

Authored with AI assistance (Codex).

Test Plan:
```bash
podman exec triton-pin-202417 bash -c 'source /data/users/warrdeng/triton-pin/ci-202417/container_env.sh
python /data/users/warrdeng/triton-pin/pytorch-cache-transport/agent_space/verify_cache_transport.py'
spin quicklint
lintrunner -a
```
64 focused cases pass with each full native old/candidate Triton pin on
H100/CUDA13.2 using the changed Python module/tests on the e6fb976 native
PyTorch wheel. Independent source controls verify rejection without writes
and successful corrected retry. Fresh-build CI remains pending.
